WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.329 --> 00:00:05.720
the shaman wherever and whenever

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.780
he or she does their shamanising

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:13.790
the shaman is a person who is able to transcend

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:19.090
the dimensional confines of cultural existence 

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.080
the people they serve are

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.960
like children within the game of culture

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.859
only the shaman knows that culture is a game, everyone else takes it seriously

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.560
that's how he can do his magic

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:38.360
you could always tell the shaman, because first of all: he usually didn't come out to see who was there

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:42.420
even though no one ever came, even though these people had visitors once every six months

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.520
the guy who wouldn't come out of his hut

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.960
for the only event in six months, was inevitably the shaman 

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.860
and when you met him

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:57.920
he wasn't interested in your velcro, or your break-apart glow-in-the-dark little trampettes 

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.680
or any of the rest of it

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.620
he was looking straight at you

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.880
through the eyes

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.700
outside of culture

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.020
saying 'what kind of a person are you?'

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:09.480
'are you a fool?'

00:01:09.481 --> 00:01:11.361
'or are you a clever fella?'

00:01:11.361 --> 00:01:13.640
'what is your measure'

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.340
'how much of the situation do you understand?'

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:22.020
'how many levels are you simultaneously aware of' 

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.340
'at this moment?'

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:30.020
and, you know, looking into the eyes of that sort of person, you either grow or turn away

